  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Jet-Age Ticket Wallet",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Jet-Age Ticket Wallet\"**\n\nSift is a wallet of airline coupons. Each customer ticket is a white coupon ruled in carrier-navy hairlines, with a stub that carries its number, perforations that tear it into sections, and tabs that sit on its top edge like folder tabs. A reply is not a toast or a checkmark: it is a rotated rubber stamp (SENT, with who and when) on a lilac carbon copy. State is applied to the paper, never hidden: closed tickets are stamped VOID, errors and 404s are void coupons, and disabled controls go dashed rather than vanishing.\n\nThe room is stock-white and navy, dense and calm, built for an agent who keeps it open all shift. A navy header band with a jet-red speed stripe frames everything; below it, the work surface is flat paper with one quiet coupon shadow. Colour is rationed: navy is the voice, carbon purple speaks only for real data (numbers, times, counts), and jet red is the alarm and the send. Condensed airline caps label every tab, stamp and field; one grotesk body carries the prose; a mono face carries the numerals.\n\nIt explicitly rejects the grey SaaS sidebar-and-feed helpdesk: no left nav column of icons, no card soup, no gradient chrome, no spinners.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy hairline coupons on a warm stock-white ground; flat, with one soft coupon shadow.",
      "Chamfered tabs on coupon heads and on the header band.",
      "Dashed perforations with half-circle notches split coupon sections and stubs.",
      "Rubber stamps (rotated, double-ruled) for status; small ruled stamps for status in lists.",
      "Carbon-purple tabular mono numerals for every ticket number, age, time and count.",
      "Jet red rationed to send, HIGH urgency, VOID/closed, and the band's speed identity.",
      "Lucide line icons at 1.5 stroke, 14-16px."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Rationed Red Rule",
        "body": "Jet red marks what must happen now (send, HIGH, VOID) and the band's identity. Never use it for decoration, links, generic primary actions or hover states.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Carbon purple in tabular mono is reserved for real data. If a value is not a number, id, time or count, it is not carbon.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The AA Pair Rule",
        "body": "Every text/background pair is documented at WCAG AA or better in globals.css. Red text on light grounds uses jet-ink; white text on jet is 5.0:1.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Caps Label, Sentence Body Rule",
        "body": "If it names a thing, it is condensed caps; if a person wrote it, it is sentence-case Barlow. Do not set prose in caps or labels in body type.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Lift Rule",
        "body": "Paper does not float. Hover changes border and tint, never shadow; only popovers rise.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put every ticket in a coupon: navy hairline, 4px corners, tabs on top, perforation between sections.",
      "Do set every number, id, time and count in carbon tabular mono (`.num`).",
      "Do show state as a stamp: ruled stamps in lists, rotated rubber stamps on the open coupon, VOID for closed and errors.",
      "Do keep red to send, HIGH, VOID/closed and the band identity, and use jet-ink for red text.",
      "Do label in condensed caps (0.06-0.08em) and write prose in sentence-case Barlow.",
      "Do keep transitions to 150-160ms ease-out colour changes; the stamp landing is the only authored motion, and reduced motion removes it.",
      "Do use Lucide icons at 1.5 stroke, 14-16px."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't build a grey SaaS sidebar-and-feed helpdesk layout.",
      "Don't use spinners; use the skeleton shimmer.",
      "Don't hide unavailable actions; show them dashed with a reason.",
      "Don't add shadows on hover or new elevation levels beyond coupon and pop.",
